This directory contains code adapted from paseo-supervision
(https://github.com/hoangnb24/paseo-supervision), source commit
1bad19b8ee6c58482494f56a3d8c6edb4f969ee1.

The upstream Work is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0); a copy is at the upstream
repository root (LICENSE). Upstream carries no NOTICE file; the copyright
holder line in its LICENSE is unfilled, so attribution here names the
project and commit.

Adapted portions (structure and algorithms, not copied code):

- observer.ts — serialized queue/generation mechanics adapted from
  upstream server/observer.ts. Removed: the supervisor sync RPC, alert
  sends, and all notification delivery.
- assessment.ts — Jev Choice response handling adapted from upstream
  server/jev.ts: strict Zod schemas, unique-maximum probability
  distributions, ~1-sum validation, confidence thresholding, and
  conservative unknown mapping.
- capture.ts — the correlation idea (latest user_message boundary,
  confirmed-send evidence) informed by upstream server/communication.ts;
  per-family send extraction is original to this repository.

Modified relative to upstream: provider-aware extraction for the SLP
family registry, SLP role routing and report-route semantics, Jev
capability gating, daemon-home binding, bounded metadata-only persistence,
and removal of every notification path. See
docs/spec/supervision-integration.md for the divergence contract.
